## Technique choice
Depth + normal discontinuity pass: render the scene twice into render targets with override
materials (MeshNormalMaterial, MeshDepthMaterial RGBADepthPacking), threshold depth and normal
discontinuities per pixel, output 1-bit bytes top row first. Both passes are depth-tested scene
renders, so hidden edges stay hidden. No wireframe material, no WireframeGeometry, no line objects.
The page's `three` namespace travels through the hook (`window.__bookStill.three`), and the page
loads `src/storytime/line-art-pass.ts` through the vite dev server, so no bare `import('three')`.

